# Copy this file to .env for local work. .env is git-ignored and must stay
# that way. On Vercel these are set under Project -> Settings -> Environment
# Variables instead, never in the repository.
#
# Nothing here is a secret. The Apps Script URL is a public endpoint by
# design and the Measurement ID is visible in the page source of every site
# that uses Google Analytics. They live here so they can be changed per
# environment, not because they need hiding.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Analytics tag
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave this line out entirely and the build uses GT-5TCZ3J3C, the tag the old
# WordPress site used, so the rebuilt site reports into the same property and
# the history stays continuous.
#
# Set it to a different ID to report somewhere else.
#
# Set it to NOTHING - the line below, with no value - and the site ships with
# no analytics at all: no script, no request to Google, no cookie. That is the
# right setting for local work, and for the Preview environment in Vercel so
# review traffic never lands in the practice's real reporting.
VITE_GA_ID=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Apps Script Web App URL, ending in /exec. Only needed here to point a
# build at a different backend - src/assets/js/site-config.js already holds
# the current one as its default.
VITE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jane booking
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every "Book an appointment" button on the site points here. Leave it out and
# the build uses https://abcaestheticsllc.janeapp.com, the practice's own Jane
# page. Set it to point a preview build somewhere else.
VITE_JANE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google reCAPTCHA v3 (anti-spam on the contact forms)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO keys are needed, and they live in TWO different places:
#
#   1. The SITE key (public) goes here. It is compiled into the page, which is
#      fine - it is designed to be visible and is useless on its own.
#
#   2. The SECRET key does NOT go here and must never be committed. It goes
#      into the Apps Script project, which is where the token is verified:
#
#        Apps Script editor -> Project Settings (gear icon)
#          -> Script Properties -> Add script property
#             Property:  RECAPTCHA_SECRET
#             Value:     the secret key from the reCAPTCHA admin console
#
# Get both at google.com/recaptcha/admin -> Create -> reCAPTCHA v3, with
# abcaestheticsllc.com (and www.) as the domains.
#
# Score threshold and allowed hostnames are tuned in apps-script/Config.gs
# under RECAPTCHA, not here.
#
# Leave this empty and nothing is loaded and nothing is enforced - which is
# what keeps local development and the offline test suite working without a
# Google account. CAPTCHA becomes active only once BOTH keys are set.
VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
